; The installed-state files (Tier 5 step 5-5; DECISIONS G445; docs/PACKAGE-MANAGER.md §8). Each
; is one Logos deterministic-CBOR value; pm/installed.nim reads and writes both, and checks each on
; every load against this text, then what it embeds against the pinned PACKAGE MANAGER App A types.
; A supporting schema, resolved against itself and the common schema only: the App A types are
; carried as bytes or text and checked apart, so that no name here is a logos. one (BCP-0104).
; Closed: an unknown field is refused. The rules the schema cannot say are pm/installed.nim's.

; <state_dir>/install/r/<rid>/m/record.<generation>: one installed record. `record` is the
; deterministic-CBOR encoding of the exact PACKAGE MANAGER §5 installed_package_record (App A),
; its `local_path`s relative to the record's `a/` directory: they are
; the selected variant's artifact paths, and the store makes them absolute from the current state
; directory at each load. `generation` counts the record files of one rid, from 1; a signer
; replacement writes the next one (PKG-0608). `archive_digest` is the BLAKE3-256 of the archive
; the record was installed from, for diagnostics only.
lcn.pm_installed_record = {
  format: 1,
  record: bstr,
  generation: uint64,
  archive_digest: bstr .size 32,
}

; <state_dir>/install/index: the committed set. Replacing it is the commit (G445). `sequence`
; counts the commits so far. `records` is sorted by package name UTF-8 bytes, then version text
; bytes; each identity and each rid once (by rule). The identity is here so that a start can name
; a record whose file is missing or unreadable.
lcn.pm_installed_index = {
  format: 1,
  sequence: uint64,
  records: [* lcn.pm_index_entry],
}

; One committed record: its directory (32 lowercase hexadecimal digits, by rule), the generation
; of its record file, and its identity, which App A's package_identity governs (by rule).
lcn.pm_index_entry = {
  rid: tstr .size 32,
  generation: uint64,
  package: tstr,
  version: tstr,
}
